Timing observations since 2001 August 14 have resulted in the measurement of 22 times of arrivals. We fitted these using the TEMPO software package3 to derive the timing model given in Table 1. The post-fit timing residuals are featureless, with no evidence for a binary companion, timing noise or period glitches. The surface dipole magnetic field strength inferred from Eq. 1 is 9.4\\times 10^{13} G, the largest by far among known radio pulsars. The pulsar is apparently young, with a characteristic age (assuming magnetic-dipole spin-down) of 83 kyr. There is no cataloged supernova remnant associated with this pulsar (Green, 2002).

